    "problem_statement": "Missing is_eye method breaks styled QR code generation\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to generate styled QR codes with custom module drawers or color masks, an AttributeError is raised because the `is_eye` method is missing from the base image classes.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image.styledpil import StyledPilImage\nfrom qrcode.image.styles import moduledrawers, colormasks\n\n# Try to create a styled QR code with a custom drawer\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, module_drawer=moduledrawers.CircleModuleDrawer())\n```\n\nThis raises:\n```\nAttributeError: 'StyledPilImage' object has no attribute 'is_eye'\n```\n\nThe same error occurs when using color masks:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image.styledpil import StyledPilImage\nfrom qrcode.image.styles import colormasks\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nmask = colormasks.SolidFillColorMask()\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, color_mask=mask)\n```\n\nAlso fails with the same AttributeError."
